      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The question asks for bias, RMSE, correlation and a model ranking on the WOA23 1° grid using landsea_01, so one common mask must be built over all fields and applied to every model.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Regrid the three models and WOA23 to the 1° grid, build ONE mask with `build_comparison_mask` over all four fields, apply it with `.where(mask)` before any metric, and score every model on that same sample. Do not rank on pairwise masks.",
        "WOA23 is part of this comparison, so `ocean_only=True` (the default) applies, with the landsea_01 ocean test (value > 1) that the question gives. Report the cell counts the mask records. Take the mean model, mean WOA23 and bias from the `compute_difference_metrics` output (`mean_data`, `mean_reference`) on this shared sample. These differ from the native-grid global means, and the answer must say so."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global means over each model's own native ocean grid must be area-weighted with areacello over the top level, which this fragment specifies.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The surface mean is Σ tos · areacello / Σ areacello over valid ocean cells only (`compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'`). Mask the weights to the same cells as the data, and do not use an unweighted mean.",
        "For the regridded comparison, `compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default. For the pattern correlation, `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`. Keep missing cells out of every denominator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Global means are computed natively with each model's areacello, and regridding to the WOA23 grid is done only for the maps and the pattern comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the native global means (Figure 2) on each model's own grid with its own `areacello`. Regrid to the 1° WOA23 grid only for the maps, bias, RMSE and correlation. State which numbers come from which grid.",
        "Use 'conservative' in `regrid_horizontal` (going to a coarser grid, and before area-weighted steps). State the method, because RMSE and correlation depend on it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "tos is a top-cell bulk potential temperature, not a skin temperature, which matters when it is compared with WOA23 0 m temperature.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the top-cell bulk temperature, and the top cell is 0–10 m for CESM2, 0–2 m for GFDL-ESM4 and 0–12 m for MPI-ESM1-2-LR. Compared with the WOA23 0 m value this is a like-for-like surface definition, but note the differing thicknesses.",
        "Sea-ice cells carry under-ice water temperature near freezing (about −1.8 °C) and are not missing. Keep them in the global means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI are native curvilinear (gn) while GFDL-ESM4 is gr (regridded to 1°), which affects masks and how the native-grid global means are computed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` (regridded from tripolar to a 1x1 degree archive grid), so its \"native\" numbers are on that 1° grid with a regridded land–sea mask. CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are `gn`. State this when describing the \"native\" means."
      ]
    },
